{
  "title": "Medplum \u2014 healthcare (2,369\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Medplum\nDomain: healthcare | Scale: large | Stars: 2,369\nProblem: Medplum is a developer platform that enables rapid development of compliant healthcare applications by providing FHIR-based infrastructure, authentication, clinical data repository, and pre-built UI components.\nTarget users: Healthcare software developers, Healthcare organizations, EHR/EMR system builders, Healthcare app developers\nCore features: FHIR-based Clinical Data Repository (CDR); OAuth/OpenID/SMART-on-FHIR Authentication; GraphQL and REST API for healthcare data; Medplum Bots for server-side application logic; React UI component library for healthcare apps; Web application for data viewing and workflow management; On-premise agent for hybrid deployments\nIntegrations: FHIR standard, SMART-on-FHIR, OAuth 2.0 / OpenID Connect, AWS Lambda, AWS CDK\nTech stack: React with TypeScript + Node.js with Express and TypeScript + PostgreSQL + AWS (Lambda, CDK), Redis for caching and background jobs\nKey libraries: Express, React, TypeScript, PostgreSQL, Redis, Jest, Turbo, Babel, ESBuild\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Monorepo structure with Turbo for build orchestration enables managing multiple interconnected packages (core, app, server, CLI, bots) from a single repository\n- Heavy emphasis on compliance and standards: FHIR adherence, HIPAA compliance, SOC2 certification, and OpenSSF Best Practices demonstrate healthcare-grade security and governance\n- Full-stack TypeScript strategy reduces context switching and enables code sharing between frontend and backend, particularly evident in shared core library and type definitions\n- Extensibility through Bots and serverless Lambda integration allows customers to add custom business logic without managing infrastructure",
